Now MainActivity.java. Need directory. Also assets/www build copy.

Write Java carefully. Packages: `com.soullink.undertalelauncher`.

Consider `WebViewClient.shouldInterceptRequest` for range requests? Not needed.

`WebResourceResponse` constructor `(String mimeType, String encoding, int statusCode, String reasonPhrase, Map<String,String> responseHeaders, InputStream data)` is API 21.

Security: path canonicalization. Assets path: use `getAssets().open("www" + path)`; path from URI can contain encoded traversal. Normalize:
```java
String clean = path.replace('\\','/');
while (clean.contains("..")) clean = clean.replace("..", "");
```
Prevent null.

Cache path: token is our own generated id + "-" + name. JS gets URL `/__cache__/<urlencoded name>`. When storing, Java generates `id + "-" + safeName`; on intercept decode last path segment. Uri.getLastPathSegment() decodes. Ensure file is inside cacheDir/mods.

MIME from filename.

Download: 
```java
@JavascriptInterface
public void downloadFile(final String url, final String fileName, final String requestId) {
  final String id = sanitizeId(requestId);
  new Thread(() -> { ... }, "soul-link-download").start();
}
```
Max 250MB, free space checks maybe.

HttpURLConnection:
```java
HttpURLConnection conn = (HttpURLConnection) new URL(url).openConnection();
conn.setInstanceFollowRedirects(true);
conn.setConnectTimeout(30000);
conn.setReadTimeout(90000);
conn.setRequestProperty("User-Agent", "Mozilla/5.0 ... SoulLinkAndroid/1.0");
conn.setRequestProperty("Accept", "*/*");
```
Note: GameBanana might reject non-browser UA? curl worked. Use a normal Chrome UA plus suffix.

Redirect across protocols handled by HttpURLConnection; it follows by default, including HTTPS? Java's HttpURLConnection follows same-protocol redirects only? Actually HttpURLConnection follows redirects for same protocol; for http→https it may not. Here https→https. Fine.

`conn.getResponseCode()` 200. contentLength.

Write to temp `.part`, then rename.

Names: `System.currentTimeMillis() + "-" + safe`? JS needs URL from callback, so Java can use `id + "-" + safe`. Sanitize id alnum/hyphen.

`safeFileName`: replace non `[A-Za-z0-9._-]` with `_`, limit 80, fallback mod.bin.

After done: local URL `ORIGIN + "/__cache__/" + Uri.encode(storedName)`.

Call JS:
```java
private void callJs(String fn, String... args) {
  StringBuilder sb = new StringBuilder("window.SLAndroidBridge&&window.SLAndroidBridge.");
  sb.append(fn).append('(');
  for (int i=0;i<args.length;i++) { if(i>0) sb.append(','); sb.append(JSONObject.quote(args[i]==null?"":args[i])); }
  sb.append(");");
  webView.post(() -> webView.evaluateJavascript(sb.toString(), null));
}
```
Progress with numbers: overload `callJsNumbers`. Keep simple strings and JS Number().

`openExternal`: validate scheme http/https, then ACTION_VIEW.

`exitApp`: runOnUiThread(this::finish).

`toast`? not necessary.

`onBackPressed` deprecation: override still works. Add `@Override public void onBackPressed()`. For API 33+ with `enableOnBackInvokedCallback` not set, legacy works. Compile target 35 with deprecation warning only.

`onPause`/`onResume`: webView.onPause/onResume; pause audio? Add `webView.onPause()` and `SL.game.pause`? Could call JS:
```java
if (SLAndroidBack...) no.
```
Add `webView.onPause(); webView.pauseTimers();` in onPause, resume in onResume. `pauseTimers()` pauses all WebViews globally; fine single.

But pausing timers while downloading? Native thread unaffected. JS promise callback may be delayed until resume. Fine.

Fullscreen: `applyImmersive()`.

Splash: theme.

Also set `setLayerType`? no.

`onCreate`:
```java
super.onCreate(savedInstanceState);
getWindow().addFlags(FLAG_KEEP_SCREEN_ON);
...
if (Build.VERSION.SDK_INT >= 21) { getWindow().setStatusBarColor(Color.TRANSPARENT); ... }
